  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Data prop",
      "text": "`SegmentedControl` support two different data formats:\n\n1. An array of strings – used when `value` and `label` are the same\n2. An array of objects – used when `value` and `label` are different",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disabled",
      "text": "To disable `SegmentedControl` item, use array of objects `data` format and set `disabled: true`\non the item that you want to disable. To disable the entire component, use `disabled` prop.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "React node as label",
      "text": "You can use any React node as label:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Color",
      "text": "By default, `SegmentedControl` uses `theme.white` with shadow in light color scheme and `var(--mantine-color-dark-6)` background color for indicator.\nSet `color` prop to change indicator `background-color`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Transitions",
      "text": "Change transition properties with:\n\n- `transitionDuration` – all transitions duration in ms, `200` by default\n- `transitionTimingFunction` – all transitions timing function, `ease` by default",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "readOnly",
      "text": "Set `readOnly` prop to prevent value from being changed:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility and usability",
      "text": "`SegmentedControl` uses radio inputs under the hood, it is accessible by default with no extra steps required if you have text in labels.\nComponent support the same keyboard events as a regular radio group.\n\nIn case you do not have text in labels (for example, when you want to use `SegmentedControl` with icons only),\nuse [VisuallyHidden](/core/visually-hidden) to make component accessible:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
